      "writtenOn": "2022-03-17T12:52:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "More generally, would it make sense (and be possible) to change this check to cover the first API level rather than the KeyMint version?\n\nAIUI:\na) ID attestation is mandatory for devices that first ship with T\nb) KeyMint v2 is first present in T\n\nThis function checks for b) -- if a device reports KeyMint v2, then a) is assumed to be true and ID attestation is mandated.  \n\nBut would it be better/more direct just to check a) via something like `get_property(\"ro.vendor.api_level\") \u003e\u003d 33`?  \n\nThat would cover a device that first shipped with T but had KeyMint v1 in it (which should support ID attestation). \n\n(OTOH, what about a device that first shipped with S, but which has its KeyMint upgraded to v2 on upgrade to T -- is that required to support ID attestation or not?)",
      "parentUuid": "030de5b6_31e0951e",
      "revId": "c200c731d83cd97968c46c8622f6e0e264d73340",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "86d3a082_2ba38f0a",
        "filename": "security/keymint/aidl/vts/functional/KeyMintAidlTestBase.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 1
      },
      "lineNbr": 210,
      "author": {
        "id": 1078064
      },
      "writtenOn": "2022-03-17T13:52:19Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I second David\u0027s suggestion, we should check the device\u0027s first API level:\nro.product.first_api_level (not ro.vendor.api_level).\nIt will cover devices shipped with T.\n\nFor the sake of coverage, I suggest we OR the two conditions:\n(1) device shipped with T (as determined from looking at ro.product.first_api_level)\n(2) Devices with KeyMint 2.\nOtherwise we will not have any devices currently running the tests (until Pixel 2022 devices come online).\n\nI agree there may be an issue with devices upgrading to T and having their KeyMint version updated, but I would prefer having test coverage now and granting exceptions to such devices later (as it\u0027s uncommon for OEMs to update their KeyMint version).",
      "parentUuid": "d48a2b9d_c2ae07dc",
      "revId": "c200c731d83cd97968c46c8622f6e0e264d73340",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
